Package: tree-sitter-cli
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armhf i386
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: command-line tool for developing Tree-sitter parsers
 Tree-sitter is a parser generator tool and an incremental parsing library. It
 can build a concrete syntax tree for a source file and efficiently update the
 syntax tree as the source file is edited.
 .
 This package contains the Tree-sitter CLI, which is used to generate, build,
 test and use Tree-sitter grammars: it can scaffold a grammar repository,
 generate parsers, run corpus tests, parse, query, highlight and tag files,
 and serve a web playground.
 .
 The command provided by this package is "tree-sitter".
 .
 Some commands need tools that are not installed automatically: building or
 testing a parser needs a C compiler (e.g. gcc), and "tree-sitter generate"
 runs grammar.js with node unless "--js-runtime native" selects the built-in
 QuickJS runtime.
